    <bpmn:process id="W_W5499" name="W5499. Director Induction, Onboarding &amp; Continuing Board Education Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Election/appointment of a new director or officer-director (per W1727); (b) annual board calendar; (c) material regulatory/governance change
Frequency: New-director onboarding: 1–3 events/year (board refresh cycle); continuing education: annual board retreat + quarterly 30–45-min regulatory briefings; per-committee deep-dives 1–2/year
Volume: All directors and committee members of the 5-entity group (board and committee rosters per VS-36.1 governance records; ~10–15 participants per session); ~6–10 board meetings/year whose agendas this program feeds (W1714)
Owner: Corporate Secretary
Participants: Board Chair, CEO, CFO, CHRO, Head of Internal Audit (VS-21), external counsel/advisers, external director-education providers, site hosts (store/DC leadership)
Source: workflow W5499 — Director Induction, Onboarding &amp; Continuing Board Education Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5499_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5499_Lane1" name="Corporate Secretary">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5499_Lane2" name="Head of Internal Audit">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5499_Lane3" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5499_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5499_Start5" name="(a) Election/appointment of a new director or officer-director (per W1727); (b) annual…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task6" name="New-director onboarding pack &amp; program: group/entity structure (5 legal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: New-director onboarding pack &amp; program: group/entity structure (5 legal entities incl. the property company VS-97 and captive VS-153), governance charter and committee charters, code of ethics &amp; conflict-of-interest policy (W1734), delegation-of-authority matrix (W1732), D&amp;O insurance briefing (VS-26), recent board minutes and standing resolutions, and the current strategy pack (VS-33); scheduled within 30 days of election/appointment per W1727
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 3–5 days preparation; 1–2 days delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task7" name="Executive &amp; functional immersion: structured meetings with CEO, CFO, CHRO, Head…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Executive &amp; functional immersion: structured meetings with CEO, CFO, CHRO, Head of Internal Audit, and VP Legal; one-day site immersion — one operating store, one DC (VS-04), and the store-support functions (VS-177 field leadership as host) — to ground oversight in frontline reality
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary / Executives
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 days/new director</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task8" name="Fiduciary &amp; regulatory education: duties of care/diligence/loyalty…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fiduciary &amp; regulatory education: duties of care/diligence/loyalty, confidentiality and insider-information handling, related-party transaction duties (W1720), SEC reportorial obligations (W1718), and exposure briefings on competition law (VS-129), anti-graft constraints around B2G sales (VS-46/VS-86), data privacy (W1735), and election-period conduct (VS-132)
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary / External Counsel
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 0.5–1 day/new director + refreshers</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task9" name="Risk &amp; controls immersion: ERM top risks and appetite (W122), internal-audit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Risk &amp; controls immersion: ERM top risks and appetite (W122), internal-audit plan and open findings (VS-21), fraud/ethics/speak-up program (VS-119), BCP and catastrophe exposure (VS-26/VS-69), and cyber posture (VS-27.3) — the same risk picture the Audit Committee receives (W1721)
Responsible (R): Head of Internal Audit / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk-function
Accountable (A): Audit Committee Chair
Duration: 0.5 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task10" name="Financial &amp; commercial deep-dive: P&amp;L drivers and store-level economics (W1405…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Financial &amp; commercial deep-dive: P&amp;L drivers and store-level economics (W1405 pattern), capex program and post-investment reviews (VS-40), treasury &amp; financing structure (VS-18), tax posture (VS-79), and the merchandise/supply-chain operating model (VS-01/VS-02) at board-literacy depth
Responsible (R): CFO / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 0.5–1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task11" name="Continuing-education calendar: annual board retreat (strategy + governance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Continuing-education calendar: annual board retreat (strategy + governance themes, tied to the Q4 meeting per W1714); quarterly 30–45-min regulatory briefings assembled from the regulatory-change horizon scan (VS-22.3) and government-affairs intelligence (VS-104); external director-education programs/seminars for independent directors budgeted annually
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: ~2 days/board-year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task12" name="Records, evaluation &amp; feedback linkage: attendance and completion logged in the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Records, evaluation &amp; feedback linkage: attendance and completion logged in the board portal (records per W1719); session feedback feeds the annual governance self-assessment (W1730) and committee-effectiveness review (W1721); the education plan and completion record are disclosable governance artifacts
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 2–3 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5499_Task13" name="Annual program review: gap analysis against self-assessment results, regulatory…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Annual program review: gap analysis against self-assessment results, regulatory developments, and board feedback; next-year plan and budget approved with the governance calendar
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary / CHRO
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 1–2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5499_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5499_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5499_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5499_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-349 (ensure controlled execution — Board Meeting Management &amp; Corporate Records (PA-36.1).)
Owner: Corporate Secretary</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5499_Assoc16" sourceRef="W5499_Annotation15" targetRef="W5499_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
