    <bpmn:process id="W_W5544" name="W5544. Emergency Executive Succession &amp; Decision-Rights Continuity Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Death, sudden medical incapacitation, immediate-effect resignation, or board removal of the CEO or any C-level executive; or the simultaneous unavailability of a quorum-critical set of officers (e.g. CEO + CFO) in a single event
Frequency: Rare; realistically &lt; 1 C-level event per decade; the succession register and tabletop are exercised annually
Volume: 1 event × the decision-rights surface across 5 legal entities (signing authorities, bank mandates, BIR-accredited and eFPS-authorized signatories, SEC/GIS officer records, board quorum, ERP approval chains) × ~6,932 employees whose payroll, approvals and reporting lines route through the affected office
Owner: Board Chair / CEO / Corporate Secretary
Participants: Board Chair, Corporate Secretary, Nomination/Governance function per W1721, CFO, CHRO, VP Legal, affected-function deputies, Treasury (bank mandates per W317), Tax Manager (BIR signatory continuity), IT (access/approval-workflow reassignment), IR (disclosure), Communications (W855/W134 discipline)
Source: workflow W5544 — Emergency Executive Succession &amp; Decision-Rights Continuity Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5544_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5544_Lane1" name="Corporate Secretary">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5544_Lane2" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5544_Lane3" name="CHRO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5544_Lane4" name="HR Benefits">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5544_Lane5" name="Nomination">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5544_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5544_Start7" name="Death, sudden medical incapacitation, immediate-effect resignation, or board removal of…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5544_Task8" name="Activation &amp; immediate board action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Activation &amp; immediate board action: Corporate Secretary convenes an emergency board meeting (telephonic/written-consent per the by-laws) within 24 hours; board appoints the pre-identified interim officer from the succession register (each C-role carries a named interim + two alternates); if the event removes the CEO, the Board Chair holds decision rights until the interim is seated
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary / Board Chair
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: &lt; 24 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5544_Task9" name="Decision-rights &amp; signing bridge">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Decision-rights &amp; signing bridge: activate the sealed delegation-of-authority matrix — interim officer assumes the role&#x27;s approval limits; Treasury re-points bank signatory mandates per W317 (dual-signatory rule preserved); Tax Manager updates BIR-accredited and eFPS-authorized signatory lists so statutory filings and payment authorizations stay valid (links to W5546&#x27;s filing-continuity concern); corporate resolutions evidencing the interim appointment generated per W1717
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary / Treasury / Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO (financial authorities) / CEO (operational authorities)
Duration: 24–72 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5544_Task10" name="ERP access &amp; approval continuity">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: ERP access &amp; approval continuity: IT re-assigns the officer&#x27;s approval-workflow roles to the interim under change control, with segregation-of-duties re-checked per W1408 (no accumulation of conflicting approvals in the rush); the vacant office&#x27;s mailbox and records preserved per W1719 retention and legal-hold rules if the event may be contested
Responsible (R): IT / Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 24–72 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5544_Task11" name="Communication rings">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Communication rings: (a) internal: executive team and direct reports first, then all-staff announcement with the interim&#x27;s authority stated; (b) external: IR runs the materiality assessment per W5017 — a CEO&#x27;s death/incapacitation or unexpected departure of a listed company is a disclosable event per W5019; lenders notified where facility agreements require officer notices; key vendors/customers contacted by the interim&#x27;s office; all external messaging rides the W855/W134 single-spokesperson discipline
Responsible (R): CHRO (internal) / IR (external) / Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): CEO / Board Chair
Duration: 24–96 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5544_Task12" name="Benefits, estate &amp; D&amp;O interface">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Benefits, estate &amp; D&amp;O interface (death/incapacitation): death-in-service benefits administered per W1325; D&amp;O and key-man insurance claims notified per the VS-26 policy machinery (W857–W864 class); executive&#x27;s family receives a single named liaison; personal-effects and estate matters handled by HR/Legal under privacy discipline
Responsible (R): HR Benefits / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5544_Task13" name="Permanent succession">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Permanent succession: the Nomination/Governance function runs the permanent search/promotion per W178 and the board&#x27;s committee process (W1721); interim-to-permanent handover documented with a decision-rights diff so no delegated authority silently persists
Responsible (R): Nomination/Governance / Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 1–6 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5544_Task14" name="Post-event review &amp; register upkeep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-event review &amp; register upkeep: within 30 days — what stalled, which delegations were exercised, signatory updates that lagged; the succession register (each C-role: named interim, alternates, sealed delegations, signatory inventory) refreshed; annual tabletop exercise scheduled with the BCP drill calendar
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5544_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5544_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5544_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5544_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-349 (ensure controlled execution — Board Meeting Management &amp; Corporate Records (PA-36.1).); CTL-231 (ensure corporate-governance compliance.) | - operational: no interim appointment proceeds without board resolution evidence (W1717) and dual-authorization on every bank/BIR signatory change | - operational: every delegation activated in an emergency is inventoried in the decision-rights diff at permanent handover
Owner: Board Chair / CEO / Corporate Secretary</bpmn:text>
